("v1695", "scalar", "Skip to the story\nA\nAaron Alderman\nThe mission\nThoughts\nMy Mind\n\nTHREADS / DAD / A SERIES FOR TEENAGERS\n\nGrowing Up in the Way of Jesus\n\nGROWING UP IN THE WAY OF JESUS\n\nFaith, courage, and becoming your own person\n\nLearning to love, think, speak, listen and take responsibility, with room for questions, mistakes, joy and change. Written directly to teenagers.\n\nStart with Room to Grow →\nDad Threads →\n\nRoom for questions, discoveries and a future of your own.\n\nONE STEP AT A TIME\n\nA way into the series.\n\nBegin with Room to Grow. The next seven articles are taking shape.\n\n01 / OPENING ARTICLE\n\nRoom to Grow\n\nJesus grew. You have room to grow too.\n\nRead Room to Grow →\n\nDraft for review\n\n02 / PLANNED\n\nQuestions Belong Here\n\nCuriosity, honest questions and faith.\n\n03 / PLANNED\n\nFinding Your Voice\n\nSpeaking honestly and listening well.\n\n04 / PLANNED\n\nDisagreeing Without Contempt\n\nConviction, respect and room to reconsider.\n\n05 / PLANNED\n\nLove That Makes Room\n\nCaring for others, prayer, rest and limits.\n\n06 / PLANNED\n\nWhen We Get Things Wrong\n\nTaking responsibility and repair; Peter and Jesus in John 21.\n\n07 / PLANNED\n\nOrdinary Good Things\n\nFriendship, meals, rest and enjoyment.\n\n08 / PLANNED\n\nA Future You Cannot Yet See\n\nHope and the next step without a complete map.\n\nAaron Alderman\n\nA few things I’ve built. A few things I’m still trying to understand.\n\nGitHub ↗\nLinkedIn ↗\nBuilt with Worldwright.io ↗\nAssurance\nLicence ↗\nChristian stewardship covenant ↗")
